LRC INDEX-THEOREM FAMILY (n=2p):  index=(p-1)/2 ; parity=p mod 4 ; method ; index!=0
  p    n  index  p%4  parity        method  !=0
  3    6      1    3     odd   Borsuk-Ulam  yes
  5   10      2    1    even   Brouwer/SOS  yes
  7   14      3    3     odd   Borsuk-Ulam  yes
 11   22      5    3     odd   Borsuk-Ulam  yes
 13   26      6    1    even   Brouwer/SOS  yes
 17   34      8    1    even   Brouwer/SOS  yes
 19   38      9    3     odd   Borsuk-Ulam  yes
 23   46     11    3     odd   Borsuk-Ulam  yes

n=14 (p=7): index=3 ODD => Borsuk-Ulam: odd-degree map S^1->S^1 has nonzero degree => antipodal
  lonely pair (t*,-t*) at the 1/14 equioscillation EXISTS. odd degree = i*sqrt7 = -trace = (p-1)/2.

INDEX THEOREM (the meta-frame): ANALYTIC index (equidist/cap=Euler char of cover) = TOPOLOGICAL index
  (Borsuk-Ulam degree). LRC(2p) <=> index != 0. p=1 mod4: Brouwer/SOS (even index); p=3 mod4: Borsuk-Ulam
  (odd index, FORCED !=0). Subsumes: cyclotomic (de Moivre deg=(p-1)/2=index), topology (Euler=top index),
  analytic (equidist=analytic index), even/odd (index parity), Vitali wall (measure vs construction),
  SOS/non-SOS (Brouwer/Borsuk-Ulam). OPEN: (1) (p-1)/2 = degree of the right map; (2) coincidence at 1/14.
